# Build & Test

This project has 3 test sets:

1. C++ Unit tests located in /test
2. Typescript API tests located in /api_tests
3. Typescript Benchmarks located in /benchmark

If a user asks to test the project without more specific instructions, this typically means "run the unit tests, then the API tests." The benchmarks are optional; include them only if being thorough.

## Unit Tests

### Install unit test dependencies

See `.github/workflows/tests.yml` for dependencies. Look for `- name: Install dependencies`

### Setup artifacts for unit tests

```sh
if [ ! -f ./test/resources/models.tar.gz ] || [ $(find ./test/resources/models.tar.gz -mtime +30 2>/dev/null | wc -l) -gt 0 ]; then
    curl https://dl.typesense.org/ci/tyrec/tyrec-1-models.tar.gz > ./test/resources/models.tar.gz
fi
```

(ignore mtime check if user asks specifically to refresh artifacts)

### Build core server binary

```sh
bazel build //:typesense-server
```

also refer to:

```sh
./ci_build_v2.sh
```

### Build/run tests

All unit tests:

```sh
bazel test //:typesense-test --cache_test_results=no --test_output=all --test_timeout=900
```

Run a specific unit test:

```sh
bazel test //:typesense-test --cache_test_results=no --test_output=all --test_timeout=30 --test_filter="*RaftServer*"
```

## API Tests

### Install API test dependencies

Refer to `.github/workflows/tests.yml` for dependencies. Look for `api-tests:`

Install bun outside of snap confinement.
https://bun.com/docs/installation

### Download API test artifacts

Refer to `.github/workflows/tests.yml` API artifacts version and replace `XX` (or cmd) below.

```sh
cd ./api-tests
mkdir -p ./artifacts
curl https://dl.typesense.org/ci/typesense/vXX-snapshot-1.tar.gz > ./artifacts/vXX-snapshot.tar.gz
tar -xzf ./artifacts/vXX-snapshot.tar.gz -C ./artifacts/
```

### Build API tests

```sh
cd api_tests && bun install && bun link
```

### Run API tests

Build core server binary as per Unit Tests section above, then find it with:

```sh
bazel cquery --output=files //:typesense-server
```

then run:

```sh
cd api_tests && TYPESENSE_BINARY_PATH="<bazel cquery path above>" TYPESENSE_DATA_DIR="./test-data" bun run src/cli.ts
```

### Troubleshooting

- If you see GLBIC errors, they are probably due to bun being installed inside snap confinement.
- Do not attempt to run Node.js as an alternative for bun.

